  "body": "**What.** A few-parameter derivation of the selection. Use the rational family, [1/1] then [L/1], as a trial solution of the D = \u221e inner equations. Impose the Stokes conditions on it, or minimize its residual, and solve for \u03c9\u221e, A, w and b. Compare with \u03c9\u221e (notes/DINF_FITS.md) and the tuned profile.\n\n**Why.** If a three- or four-parameter version reproduces \u03c9\u221e to several digits, it is the semi-analytic derivation of Eq. (16) and its parameters that the paper asks for. If not, the failure shows how many harmonics the selection needs.\n\n**Acceptance (can fail).** On a planted inner problem whose solution is exactly [1/1], the method returns the planted parameters. The real \u03c9\u221e is reported with its error against the extrapolated 2\u03c0/1.643893746, and the trend with L. No claim beyond what the trend shows.\n\n**Depends on.** #133, for the starting values.\n",
